---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Experience — Prashant Kumar" description="Experience across enterprise architecture, transformation, technology strategy and regulated utilities.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Experience</p>
      <h1>From engineering depth<br/>to enterprise perspective.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Over two decades, my work has moved from building enterprise platforms to shaping the strategies, guardrails and investment choices around them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--roomy">
    <div class="container brand-columns">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What I bring</p>
        <p class="lead-copy">Strategic architecture grounded in delivery — connecting business intent, technology choice, regulation, cost and long-term optionality.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline">
        <article><span>Now</span><div><h3>Enterprise strategy & architecture</h3><p>Advising within a regulated energy environment on customer transformation, platform direction, architecture governance, data, AI and technology investment.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>Leadership</span><div><h3>Architecture & technology advisory</h3><p>Leading complex, multi-vendor transformation work across architecture, cloud, integration and digital modernisation.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>Foundation</span><div><h3>Global technology delivery</h3><p>Engineering and architecture roles across Australia, the UK, North America, Europe and India — building the delivery judgement behind the strategy.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Global perspective</p>
        <div><h2>Experience shaped across borders.</h2><p>Working across different markets and operating cultures has shaped how I approach technology change: context matters, patterns travel imperfectly, and good architecture makes room for both.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="country-strip" aria-label="Countries where Prashant has worked">
        <span>Australia</span><span>Canada</span><span>India</span><span>Malaysia</span><span>Sweden</span><span>United Kingdom</span><span>United States</span>
      </div>
      <p class="disclosure">Current role: Enterprise Architect at SA Power Networks. Views expressed here are personal.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
